    "result_text": "Done. The build passes with all tests green.\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe rule applies to `POST /api/owners`, where `registrationDate` is an optional supplied field. I added a future-date guard at the front of the pipeline, following the project's OfficeFloor escalation pattern (functions throw checked exceptions; handlers respond).\n\n1. **`ValidateOwnerFields.java`** (first pipeline step) \u2014 before any other validation, if a `registrationDate` is supplied and is after the server's current date (`LocalDate.now()`), it throws the new checked exception. Placing it first means a future date is rejected before the 404/quota rules run, and before `BuildOwner` defaults/rolls the date forward.\n\n2. **`OwnerRegistrationDateFutureException.java`** \u2014 new checked exception (`extends Exception`) carrying the supplied and server dates.\n\n3. **`OwnerRegistrationDateFutureExceptionHandler.java`** \u2014 responds `400 Bad Request` with a JSON body, mirroring `OwnerFieldsRequiredExceptionHandler`.\n\n4. **`.../escalation/...OwnerRegistrationDateFutureException.yml`** \u2014 wires the exception to its handler.\n\nThe acceptance test `errorRejectsFutureDate` (posts `registrationDate: 2999-01-01`, expects 400) passes, and the full suite is `BUILD SUCCESS`. A supplied past/today date and an omitted date are unaffected (they still default and roll to a business day as before).",
